--TEST--
`rule:security/isolate-shares-nothing`: a literal `args:` map is compared against the method entry's parameters at compile time, with the ordinary named-argument errors
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Reports {
    public static function span(int $months, string $from): int {
        return $months;
    }
}

// A key the entry does not declare. `moths` is not a parameter.
var $typo = spawn script Reports::span with(args: ["moths" => 3, "from" => "may"]);

// A parameter the map leaves out. `from` has no entry.
var $short = spawn script Reports::span with(args: ["months" => 3]);

// No `args:` at all, so neither parameter has an entry.
var $none = spawn script Reports::span;

// Every parameter has an entry, so this spawn compiles.
var $ok = spawn script Reports::span with(args: ["months" => 3, "from" => "may"]);
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0486]: `Reports::span` has no parameter named `moths`
%A
error[E0402]: `args:` has no entry for the parameter(s) `from`
%A
error[E0402]: `args:` has no entry for the parameter(s) `months`, `from`
%A
error: aborting due to 3 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
